hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"661","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Anba Muadh bin Hisham, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “For a month he made supplication against an Arab neighborhood, then he left it.”"
"662","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of his father, he said: “I prayed behind the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. I said the salaam and he did not say the Qunoot, I prayed behind Abu Bakr but he did not say the Qunoot, I prayed behind Omar but he did not say the Qunoot, I prayed behind Uthman but he did not say the Qunoot, I prayed behind Ali, but he did not say Qunoot, then he said: O my son, this is an innovation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"663","665 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abbad told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Jabir bin Abd. God, he said: “We were praying the noon prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I would take a handful of pebbles in my palm, cool it, then transfer it to my palm.” The other, when I prostrate, I place it on my forehead.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"664","666 Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi Al-Basri told us, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Jarir, on the authority of Mutarrif, he said: “I prayed And Imran bin Husayn succeeded Ali bin Abi Talib. Whenever he prostrated, he would say “Allahu Akbar,” and when he raised his head from prostration, he would say “Allahu Akbar,” and when he got up from The two rak'ahs of takbir.\ When he finished his prayer"
"665","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Muadh told us, and Yahya told us, they said: Zuhair told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told me, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Alqamah, and Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Masoud, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say “Allahu Akbar” in every Lowering and raising, and saluting to his right and to his left.” Abu Bakr and Omar used to do that."
"666","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Bishr, he said: I heard Yusuf, who is the son of Mahak. He narrates, on the authority of a wise man, who said: “I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that I will not delay anyone but him standing.”"
"667","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adiy told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Nasr ibn Asim, on the authority of Malik ibn Al-Huwaithir saw the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “raise his hands in his prayer when he bows, and when he raises his head from his bowing, and when he prostrates, And when he raises his head from his prostration until it is in line with the branches of his ears, Anba Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna said: Abdul-Ala told us, he said: He told us Saeed, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Nasr ibn Asim, on the authority of Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, that he saw the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, raise his hands So he mentioned something similar, Anba Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Nasr bin Asim, On the authority of Malik bin Al-Huwaith, that the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, would, whenever he entered into prayer, mention something similar to it and add to it, “And when he bowed, he would do “Like that, and when he raises his head from bowing, he does the same, and if he raises his head from prostration, he does the same.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"668","670 Muhammad bin Ubaid bin Muhammad al-Kufi al-Muharbi informed us, saying: Ibn al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, On the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “would raise his hands when he opened the prayer, and when he bowed, and when he raised his hands, and he did not He does that while prostrating.\ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"669","671 Al-Hussein bin Issa Al-Qumsi Al-Bistami told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Anba Sharik, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Wael bin Hajar, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he prostrated, placing his knees before his hands, and when he stood up, he raised \His hands before his knees\"""""
"670","672 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Abdullah bin Nafi’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Hassan, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, On the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “One of you is baptized during his prayer and he is blessed as a camel is blessed,” and he once said Another: “One of you is baptized, and in his prayer he is blessed like the blessing of a camel.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"671","673 Harun bin Muhammad bin Bakkar bin Bilal told us, from his book, he said: Marwan bin Muhammad told us, he said: Abdul Aziz told us Ibn Muhammad, he said: Muhammad Ibn Abdullah told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “When one of you prostrates, let him place his hands before his knees, and do not touch the camel’s burrow.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"672","674 Ziyad bin Ayyub Dalawayh told us, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, he said: Ayyub told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he narrated it, He said: “The hands prostrate as the face prostrates, so when one of you lowers his face, let him lower his hands, and when he raises it, let him raise them.”"
"673","675 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The command of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: “He should prostrate on seven bones, and not let his hair or his clothes be tied up.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"674","676 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn al-Hadi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Aamir bin Saad, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Muttalib said that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “When a servant prostrates, seven Arabs prostrate with him: his face His hands, his knees, and his feet.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"675","677 Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, a recitation of it, and I am listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah Al-Hadi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri He said: “The eyes of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw traces of water and mud on his forehead and nose in the morning of the night of the twenty-first.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"676","678 Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh, Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala, and al-Harith ibn Miskin informed us of a reading from him, and I am listening, The word for it is, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdullah bin Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “I was commanded to prostrate on seven parts, not covering the hair or the clothes: the forehead, the nose, the hands, and the knees.” And the feet"
"677","679 Amr bin Mansour Al-Nasa’i told us, he said: Al-Mu’alla bin Asad told us, he said: Wahib told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Tawus, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I was commanded to prostrate on seven bones on the forehead, and he indicated With his hand over his nose, and the hands and knees, and the tips of the feet.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"678","680 Muhammad bin Mansour and Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Basri informed us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was commanded to prostrate on all seven, and forbade the hair and clothes to be tied up on his hands and knees. And the tips of his fingers.” Sufyan said: Ibn Tawus told us: “He put his hand on his forehead and pointed it over his nose.” He said: This is one. The word is for Muhammad (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"679","681 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam informed us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Layth, he said: Ibn Al-Had reported, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim Bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Amer Bin Saad Bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of Abbas Bin Abdul-Muttalib, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “When a servant prostrates, seven people prostrate with him: his face, his hands, his knees, and his feet.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"680","682 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Abdah, he said: Abba Ubayd Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of Al-Araj On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I missed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night, and I came to him while he was prostrating. With his feet upright, he was saying: “O God, I seek refuge in Your satisfaction from Your wrath, and in Your pardon from Your punishment. I cannot count Your praise. You Just as you praised yourself.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"681","683 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Abd al-Hamid bin Ja’far told us, he said: Muhammad bin Sa’id told us, he said: Ata’, on the authority of Abu Humaid al-Sa’idi, who said: “When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, descended to the ground in prostration, his upper arms were close to his armpits. And he opened his toes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"682","684 Ahmad bin Nasih told us, he said: Ibn Idris told us, he said: I heard Asim bin Kulayb, mentioning on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wael bin Hijr, he said: I came to Medina, and I said, “Let us look at the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” So he said “Allahu Akbar” and raised his hands until I saw his thumbs. close to his ears, so when he wanted to bow, he said the takbir and raised his hands, then he raised his head and said: God hears those who praise Him, then he said the takbir and prostrated, So his hands were from his ears to the place where he faced the prayer.”"
"683","685 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Yazid is the son of Harun, he said: Abu Al-Ala told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “None of you should spread his arms while prostrating like a dog.”"
"684","686 Ali bin Hajar Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Anba Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: Al-Bara’ described prostration for us, so he placed his hands on the ground. And he raised his crotch and said: This is what I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"685","687 Abdah bin Abd al-Rahim told us, he said: Abba Ibn Shumail, he said: Abba Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of al-Baraa, that the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was “when he prayed, he would commit a misdemeanor.”"
"686","688 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Bakr told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abdullah bin Malik Ibn In addition, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he prayed, he would spread his hands together until the whites of his armpits were visible.”"
"687","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ informed us, saying: Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Bashir bin Forbidden, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “If you had been in the presence of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, you would have seen his armpits.” Abu Majliz said: It is as if he said that because he was in prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"688","690 Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: I am Ismail, he said: Dawud told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Aqram, on the authority of his father, He said: “I prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I could see the chastity of his armpits when he prostrated.”"
"689","691 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Layth, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hilal, On the authority of Ja`far bin Abdullah, that Tamim bin Mahmoud told him, that Abdul Rahman bin Shibl told him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He forbade three things: “The pecking of a crow, the nesting of wild animals, and a man setting a place for prayer, just as a camel positions itself.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"690","692 Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of his uncle Yazid, on the authority of Maimuna, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, used to “when he prostrated, he would keep his hands together, even if an animal wanted to pass under his hands, it would.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"691","693 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Abdah, he said: Sa`id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, and Abba Ismail bin Masoud, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Anas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Be moderate in Prostration, and do not let any of you spread out his arms like a dog.” The wording is from Ishaq."
"692","694 Ali bin Khashram Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Anba Issa, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abu Masoud, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A prayer is not sufficient in which a man does not straighten his cross while bowing and prostrating.”"
"693","695 Humayd bin Masada told us, on the authority of Yazid, he said: Shu`bah and Rawh told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I was commanded to prostrate on seven, and not to tie up my hair or my clothes.”"
"694","696 Amr bin Al-Aswad bin Amr Al-Sarhi told us, he said: Abba Ibn Wahb, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith told us, that Bukair narrated to him, that Kurayb, the client of Ibn Abbas, narrated to him, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, that he saw Abdullah bin Al-Harith with his head tied behind him, So he got up and started to untie it. When he left, he went to Ibn Abbas and said: What do you have with my head? He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The example of one who prays with his head bowed is like the one who prays with his head folded.”"
"695","697 Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Makki informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded He, peace and blessings be upon him, prostrated on seven bones, and he forbade making one’s hair and clothes untwisted. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"696","698 Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Anba Abdullah, on the authority of Khalid bin Abdul Rahman, he said: Ghalib al-Qattan narrated to me, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Muzani, on the authority of Anas, said: “When we prayed behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the backs, we would prostrate on our clothes out of fear. \The free one\"""""
"697","699 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Abdah, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: “Complete your bowing and prostration. By God, I see you behind my back in your bowing and prostration.”"
"698","700 Abu Dawud Sulaiman bin Saif told us, he said: Abu Ali al-Hanafi told us, and Uthman bin Omar told us, Abu Ali said: he told us, and he said Othman: Dawud bin Qais informed us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Hunayn, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ali bin Abi A student said: My love forbade me from three things. I do not say that He forbade people: “about wearing gold seals, about wearing a bow, and about combed turbans.” I do not recite while prostrating or bowing.”"
"699","701 Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh informed us, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, and Yunus and Al-Harith bin Miskin informed me, reading about it, and I was hearing, about Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Ibrahim bin Abdullah told me that his father told him that he heard Ali, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me “to recite while bowing or prostrating.”"
"700","702 Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Sulayman bin Suhaim told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Ma’bad. Ibn Abbas, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, removed the curtain while his head was tied while he was sick. In which he died, and he said: “O God, have I conveyed to me three times that nothing remains of the glad tidings of prophecy except the good vision that the servant sees, or You see, I have been forbidden from reciting while bowing and prostrating, so when you kneel, glorify the Lord, and when you prostrate, strive to supplicate. “It is certain that you will be answered.”"
"701","703 Hannad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Sa’id bin Masruq, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Abu Rushdin, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I spent the night at my aunt Maymunah bint Al-Harith, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spent the night. Then I saw him getting up to fulfill his needs. So he came to the waterskin and untied it, so he performed ablution, an ablution between two ablutions, then he went to his bed and fell asleep, then he got up again and came. He untied the waterskin, then he performed ablution, which is the proper ablution, then he stood up to pray, and he used to say during his prostration: “O God, put light in my heart. And put light in my hearing, and put light in my sight, and put light beneath me, and light above me, and light on my right, and light on my left, and put light in front of me Light, and put light behind me, and give me greater light.” Then he slept until he blew, then Bilal came to him and woke him up for prayer."
"702","704 Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Anba Abdullah, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say in his bowing and prostration: “Glory be to You, O God, our Lord, and with Your praise, O God, forgive me.” He interprets the Qur’an"
"703","705 Muhammad bin Qudamah told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, he said: Aisha said: I lost a messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out of his bed, so I started to touch him, and I thought that he had come to one of his female slaves, so my hand fell on him while he was prostrating. He says: “O God, forgive me for what I have concealed and what I have declared.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"704","706 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: I lost the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I thought he had come to some of his female slaves, so I looked for him, and lo, He was prostrating and saying: “Lord, forgive me for what I have concealed and what I have declared.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"705","707 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Abi Salamah told us, he said: My uncle told me Al-Majishun bin Abi Salama, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Al-Araj, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Ali, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And when he prostrated, he would say: “O God, to You I prostrated, and to You I submitted, and in You I believed. My face prostrated to the One who created it and shaped it, so it became good.” He formed him, and improved his hearing and sight. Blessed be God, the best of creators.”"
"706","708 Yahya bin Uthman told us, he said: Abu Haywa told us, he said: Shuaib bin Abi Hamza told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, On the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in a similar way, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to say in his prostration: “O God, I prostrate to You, and to You I believed, and I submitted to you, and you are my Lord. My face prostrated to the One who created it, shaped it, and opened its hearing and sight. Blessed be God. \the creators\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"707","709 Yahya bin Uthman told us, he said: Ibn Himyar told us, he said: Shuaib told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, and he mentioned another Before him, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz al-Araj, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Maslamah, that whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose He prays voluntarily. When he prostrates, he says: “O God, to You I have prostrated, and in You I have believed, and to You I have submitted. O God, you are my Lord, my face has prostrated to the One who created it. And shaped him, and improved his hearing and his sight. Blessed be God, the best of creators.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"708","710 Sawar bin Abdullah bin Sawar Al-Qadi and Ibn Bashar told us, on the authority of Abdul Wahhab, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say about prostrating the Qur’an at night: “My face prostrates to the One who created it. He strengthened his hearing and sight, with his might and strength.”"
"709","711 Ishaq told us, he said: Abba Jarir, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I lost the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night I found him prostrating with his feet facing the Qiblah, and I heard him say: I seek refuge in Your pleasure from... Your anger, and I seek refuge in you to recover from your punishment, and I seek refuge in you from you, I do not praise you, you are as you praised yourself.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"710","712 Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say in his bowing and prostration: “Glory be to You, O God, our Lord, and to You be praise, O God, forgive me.” He interprets the Qur’an"
"711","713 Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan Al-Masisi told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, he said: Ibn Abi told me Malika, on the authority of Aisha, said: I lost the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night, and I thought that he had gone to some of his wives. So I felt for him, and he was kneeling or prostrating, saying: “Glory be to You and with Your praise, there is no god but You.” So I said: May my father be sacrificed for you, I am in a matter. And you are in another place"
"712","714 Harun bin Abdullah told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Siwar told us, he said: Laith told us, on the authority of Muawiyah, on the authority of Amr bin Qais, He heard Asim bin Humaid saying: I heard Awf bin Malik saying: I got up with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he began to fast and perform ablution. Then he stood up and prayed, and he began to pray from the cow. He does not pass by a sign of mercy except that he stops and asks, and he does not pass by a sign of punishment except that he stops and seeks refuge, then He bowed and remained bowing as long as he stood, saying in his bowing: “Glory be to Him who is mighty, and of kingdom, and of pride, and of greatness.” Then he prostrated. As long as he bows, he says in his prostration: “Glory be to Him of power, kingdom, pride, and greatness,” then he recites Aal Imran, then Surah by Surah he did something like that (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"713","715 Ishaq told us, he said: Anba Jarir, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Mustadawrid, on the authority of Silah, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night. He opened Surat Al-Baqarah and recited one hundred verses. He did not bow and proceeded. I said: He should complete it. In the two rak'ahs, he continued, and I said: He should complete it and then bow, so he continued until he recited Surat An-Nisa, then Al Imran, then he bowed in the manner of his standing. He says: “Glory be to my Lord the Great, Glory be to my Lord the Great,” then he raised his head and said: “God hears those who praise Him. Our Lord, praise be to You.” He stood for a long time, then prostrated and prolonged his prostration, saying in his prostration: “Glory be to my Lord the Most High, Glory be to my Lord the Most High,” without mentioning any intimidation verse. Or glorification of God except by mentioning Him."
"714","716 Bundar bin Bashar informed us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id al-Qattan, and Ibn Abi Adiy, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Mutarrif, On the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say in his bowing and prostration: “Glory be to the Holy One, Lord of the angels and the spirit.”"
"715","717 Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Abdullah bin Ibrahim bin Omar bin Kaysan told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Wahb bin Manoos, he said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr, he said: I heard Anas, saying: I have never seen anyone’s prayer more similar to the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, from this young man, meaning Omar bin Abdul Aziz, “So we recorded ten times of praise in his bowing, and in his prostration ten times of praise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"716","718 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid Abu Yahya al-Muqri, who was a Basra, informed us. He said: My father told us. He said: Hammam told us. Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, that Ali bin Yahya bin Khallad bin Malik bin Rafi’ bin Malik told him, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His uncle, Rifa’ah bin Rafi’, said: While the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting and we were around him, when a man entered and went to the Qiblah. So he prayed, and when he finished his prayer, he came and greeted the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the people. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: And on you, go and pray, for you have not prayed.” So he went and prayed, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, began to look at his prayer, so we do not know what was wrong with it. When he finished his prayer, he came and greeted the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the people. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Go. So pray, for you have not prayed.” So he repeated it twice, or three times, and the man said: O Messenger of God, why did you find fault with my prayer? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The prayer of any of you is not complete until he performs ablution, as God Almighty commanded him, and washes it.” His face and hands up to the elbows, and he wipes his head and feet up to the ankles, then he glorifies God and praises Him and glorifies Him,” he said. Hammam: And I heard him say: “And he praises God and glorifies Him and magnifies Him.” He said: I heard both of them. He said: He said: “And he recites whatever is possible from The Qur’an is from what God taught him and permitted him to do in it, then he says “Allahu Akbar” and kneels until his joints are at ease and relaxed, then he says: “God has heard whoever Praise Him, then he stands straight until his back is straightened, then he says “Allahu Akbar” and prostrates, until he makes his face high.” And I heard him say: “His forehead until His joints are at ease and relaxed, and he says “Allahu Akbar” and rises until he is sitting level on his seat and straightening his back, then he says “Allahu Akbar” and prostrates, until He should bow his face and relax. If he does not do this, his prayer is not complete.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"717","719 Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Sumayy, that he heard Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The closest a servant is to his Lord is when he is prostrating, so supplicate often.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"718","720 Hisham bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Haql, who is the son of Ziyad al-Dimashqi, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir. On the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, he said: Rabi’ah bin Ka’b Al-Aslami told me, he said: I used to go to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. With his ablution and his need, he said: “Ask me.” I said: I accompany you in Paradise. He said: “Or something else?” I said: That is it. He said: “So I mean upon yourself with many prostrations.”"
"719","721 Al-Hussein bin Harith Abu Ammar Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Al-Walid bin Muslim told me, he said: Al-Awza’i told me, he said: Al-Walid bin Hisham Al-Mu’iti told me, he said: Ma’dan bin Talha Al-Yamari told me, he said: I met Thawban, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace be upon him, so I said: Guide me to a job that will benefit me, or admit me to Paradise, so he remained silent about me for three, then he turned to me and said: You must prostrate. For I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There is no servant who prostrates before God in a prostration except that God raises him one degree because of it, and lowers He committed a sin because of it.” Ma’dan said: Then I met Abu al-Darda’, and I asked him about what I asked Thawban about, and he said: You must prostrate, for I I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “There is no servant who prostrates before God in prostration, but God raises him one degree thereby and removes from him a sin.” \""
720"""
"720","Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn informed us at al-Massisah, from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Ma'mar and al-Nu'man ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ata' ibn Yazid, who said: I was sitting with Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id. One of them narrated the hadith of intercession, the other listening silently. He said: ""Then the angels come and intercede, and the Messengers intercede."" He mentioned the Sirat (Bridge). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""I will be the first to cross it. When Allah finishes judging between His creation and brings out of the Fire whom He wills, Allah will command the angels and Messengers to intercede. They will be recognized by their marks, for the Fire consumes every part of the son of Adam except the place of prostration. Then water of Paradise will be poured upon them, and they will grow like a seed grows in floodwater."""
"721","723 Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam al-Tarsusi told us, saying: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, he said: Tell us Muhammad bin Abi Yaqoub Al-Basri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, on the authority of his father, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out against us, in One of the evening prayers, and he was carrying Hasan or Hussein, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came forward and placed him, then he said the takbir for the prayer, prayed, and prostrated between I prayed with my back, prostrating it for a long time. My father said: I raised my head and saw the boy on the back of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was prostrating. So I returned to my prostration, and when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished the prayer, the people said: O Messenger of God, you prostrated before me in your prayer, prostrating. You delayed it until we thought that something had happened and that you were being inspired. He said: “All of that did not happen, but my son left me, and I hated to I will hasten him until he fulfills his need.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"722","724 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Dukain told us, and Yahya bin Adam told us, they said: Zuhair told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, and Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying “Allahu Akbar” in every Lowering and raising, standing and sitting, and he said salaams to his right and to his left: “Peace and mercy of God be upon you,” until I could see the white of his cheek. He said: And I saw Abu Bakr and Omar will do that.”"
"723","725 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Nasr bin Asim, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Huwaith, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he entered into prayer, and when he bowed, he did the same, and when he rose He raised his head from bowing, he did the same, and if he raised his head from prostration, he did the same, as if he meant raising his hands. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"724","726 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was, “ When he begins the prayer, he says “Allahu Akbar” and raises his hands, and when he bows, he says “Allahu Akbar” and after bowing, and he does not raise himself between the two prostrations.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"725","727 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abu Hamza, He heard him speaking on the authority of a man from Abs, on the authority of Hudhayfah, that he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he stood beside him and said: “By God “The greatest is the possessor of kingdom, might, pride, and greatness.” Then he recited with Al-Baqarah, then he bowed, and his bowing was like He stood up and said in his bowing: “Glory be to my Lord the Great, Glory be to my Lord the Great,” and he said when he raised his head: “To my Lord, praise be to my Lord, praise be to my Lord.” He used to say during his prostration: “Glory be to my Lord, the Most High,” and between the two prostrations he used to say: “My Lord, forgive me, my Lord, forgive me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"726","728 Musa bin Abdullah bin Musa Al-Basri informed us, saying: Al-Nadhar bin Kathir Abu Sahl Al-Azdi told me, he said: “He prayed beside me. Abdullah bin Tawus, in Mina, in the Al-Khaif Mosque. Whenever he prostrated the first prostration, he would raise his head from it, raising his hands facing his face. I denied that, so I said to Wahib bin Khalid: This man is doing something that I have never seen anyone do. So Wahib said to him: You are doing something that I have never seen anyone do. We saw someone making it, and Abdullah bin Tawus said: I saw my father making it, and he said: I saw Ibn Abbas making it, and Abdullah bin Abbas said I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, making it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"727","729 Abd al-Rahman bin Ibrahim Duhaym al-Dimashqi told us, he said: Marwan told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin al-Asam told us. He said: Yazid bin Al-Assam told me, on the authority of Maimunah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he prostrated, he folded his hands until the white of His armpits from behind him, and when he sits, check on his left thigh.”"
"728","730 Ubayd Allah bin Sa’id told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: Al-Hakam told me, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Al-Baraa’ said: “The prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was his bowing, his prostration, and his standing after he raised his head from bowing and between The two prostrations, close to normal.”"
"729","731 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Al-Aswad And Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to say “Allahu Akbar” every time he was raised, when he was standing, standing, and sitting, and Abu Bakr, Omar, and Othman.”"
"730","732 Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Hujain, who is Ibn al-Muthanna, told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, he said: Aqeel told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al Harith bin Hisham told me that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God was May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “When he stands to pray, he says “Allahu Akbar” when he stands, then he says “Allahu Akbar” when he bows, then he says: “Allah hears those who praise Him,” when he raises his cross. from the rak’ah, then he says while standing: Our Lord, praise be to You. Then he says “Allahu Akbar” when he descends and prostrates, then he says “Allahu Akbar” when he raises his head, then he says “Allahu Akbar” when he prostrates. He prostrates, then he says “Allahu Akbar” when he raises his head, then he does that for the entire prayer until he completes it, and he says “Allahu Akbar” when he gets up from the two after \sitting\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"731","733 Ziyad bin Ayyub Dalawayh told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Ayyub told us, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, he said: Abu came to us Sulaiman Malik bin Al-Huwayrith came to our mosque and said: I want to show you how I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying. He said: “So he sat in The first rak’ah when he raised his head from the last prostration.”"
"732","734 Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Anba Hushaym, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Huwayrith, he said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, is praying, but if he is in the odd-numbered prayer of his prayer, he does not get up until he is completely seated.”"
"733","735 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Wahhab told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, he said: Malik bin Al-Huwaithir comes to us and says: Shall I not tell you about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? So he prays at a time other than the time for prayer, so when he raises His head from the second prostration. At the beginning of the rak’ah he sat straight, then he stood up and leaned on the ground.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"734","736 Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: Anba Sharik, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wael bin Hajar said: I saw the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when he prostrated, placing his knees before his hands, and when he got up, he raised his hands before His knees.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: He did not say this on the authority of a partner other than Yazid bin Harun, and God Almighty knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"735","737 Qutaibah bin Sa’id informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah, that Abu Hurairah used to lead them in prayer, saying “Allahu Akbar.” Whenever he lowers and raises.” Then when he left, he said: By God, I resemble your prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"736","738 Nasr ibn Ali and Siwar ibn Abdullah ibn Siwar informed us, saying: Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul-Rahman, and on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul-Rahman, that they: They prayed behind Abu Hurairah, “So when he bowed he said the takbir, and when he rose He raised his head and said: God hears whoever praises, Our Lord, and to You be praise. Then he prostrated and said “Allahu Akbar,” and he raised his head and “Allahu Akbar,” then he said “Allahu Akbar” when he got up from the rak’ah. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I am the closest of you in resemblance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. This prayer continued until he left this world. “The word is for a bracelet"
"737","739 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah Ibn Omar, on the authority of his father, that he said: “Indeed, it is from the Sunnah of prayer that you prostrate your left foot and place your right foot upright.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"738","740 Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman bin Dawud told us, he said: Ishaq bin Bakr told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Yahya, Al-Qasim narrated to him, on the authority of Abdullah, who is the son of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of his father, who said: “Part of the Sunnah of prayer is to place the right foot erect.” “And facing him with her fingers toward the Qiblah, and sitting on the left.”"
"739","741 Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Issa told us, he said: Abba Ibn Al-Mubarak, he said: Abba Makhramah bin Bukair, Amer bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair told us, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he sat for two days, or The four put his hands on his knees and then pointed with his finger.”"
"740","742 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri informed us, saying: Sufyan told us, he said: Asim bin Kulayb told us, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Wael bin Hajar, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I saw him raising his hands when he began the prayer until they were in line with his shoulders. And if he wanted to kneel, and if he sat for the two rak’ahs, he would lie down with the left one and place the right one in the position of the rak’ah, and put his right hand on his right thigh. And he raised his finger in supplication, and placed his left hand on his left leg. He said: Then I came to them from Qabil and saw them raising their hands in Pyrenees (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"741","743 Ali bin Hajar informed us, saying: Abba Ishmael, who is Ibn Jafar, on the authority of Muslim bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Ali bin Abdul Rahman Al-Mu’awiyah, on the authority of Abdullah, said that he saw a man moving pebbles with his hand while he was praying. When he left, Abdullah said to him: “Do not move the pebbles.” While you are praying, that is from Satan, but do as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to do. He said: And how did he do? He said: “So he placed his right hand on his thigh, and pointed with his finger next to the thumb in the direction of the Qiblah, and looked at it, or something similar.” Then he said: This is how I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing"
"742","744 Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi informed us, on the authority of Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught us to say when we sit in the two rak’ahs: “Greetings are to God, and prayers and good deeds, peace be upon you.” O Prophet, God’s mercy and blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant. and His Messenger\ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"743","745 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq talking, on the authority of my father Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, said: We did not know what to say in every two rak’ahs other than to glorify God, glorify God, and praise our Lord, and that Muhammad knew So the beginnings and endings of goodness, and he said: “When you sit in every two rak’ahs, say: Greetings are to God, and prayers and good deeds, peace be upon you.” O Prophet, God’s mercy and blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant. \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"744","746 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abtar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught us the tashahhud in prayer, and the tashahhud in times of need, and he said: “The tashahhud in prayer: Greetings to God.” And the prayers and good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God’s mercy and blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god. Except Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.” To the end of the tashahhud, Anba Ishaq bin Ibrahim said: Yahya, who is the son of Adam, said: I heard Sufyan testify to this in the written and voluntary books, and he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Mansour and Hammad told us, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"745","747 Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh informed us, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Amr bin Al-Harith informed me, that Zaid bin Abi Anisa Al-Jazari narrated to him, that Abu Ishaq narrated to him, on the authority of Al-Aswad, and Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, he said: We were with the Messenger of We do not know anything, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: “Say in every session: Greetings and prayers are for God.” And the good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God’s mercy and blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God. And that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"746","748 Muhammad bin Jablah al-Rafiqi told us, he said: Al-Alaa bin Hilal told us, he said: Ubayd Allah, who is Ibn Amr, told us, on the authority of Zaid, On the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah ibn Qays, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: We did not know what to say when we prayed, so the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught us. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said to us: “Say: Greetings are to God and prayers and good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God’s mercy.” And His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger,” Ubaid said. By God, Zaid said: On the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, he said: I saw Ibn Masoud teaching us these words as the Qur’an teaches us. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"747","749 Abd al-Rahman bin Khalid al-Raqqi told us, saying: Harith bin Atiya told us, and he was one of the ascetics of the people, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hammad. On the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: When we prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, we would say: Peace be upon God. Peace be upon Gabriel, peace be upon Michael, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not say peace be upon God, for God is peace, but Say: Greetings are to God, and prayers and good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God’s mercy and blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. “I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, He alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"748","750 Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Ibn Masoud said: We used to pray with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we would say: Peace be upon God, peace be upon Gabriel, peace be upon Michael, so he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Do not say peace be upon God, for God is peace, but say: Greetings are due to God, prayers and good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God’s mercy and blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that “Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"749","751 Bishr bin Khaled Al-Askari told us, he said: Anba Ghandar, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Suleiman, Mansour, Hammad, and Mughirah. And Abu Hashem, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said regarding the tashahhud: “Greetings, prayers, and good things belong to God, Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God’s mercy and blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that “Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"750","752 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Al-Fadl bin Dukain, he said: Saif Al-Makki told us, he said: I heard a mujahid, saying: Abu Muammar told me, he said: I heard Abdullah saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught us the Tashahhud just as he teaches us the surah from the Qur’an. And his palm is between his hands. “Greetings are to God, and prayers and good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God’s mercy and blessings. Peace be upon us and the servants of God.” “God is the righteous, I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"751","753 Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Hisham told us, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Jubayr, on the authority of Hattan bin Abdullah, that Al-Ash’ari said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed us and taught us our Sunnah and explained to us Our prayer. He said: “Establish your rows, then let one of you lead you in prayer. When he says “Allahu Akbar”, say “Allahu Akbar”, and when he says: “Not even those who go astray”, then say “Amin”. May God revive you. And when the Imam says “Allahu Akbar” and bows, “Allahu Akbar” and bowing, for the Imam bows before you and rises before you.” The Prophet of God said: “So do that with that.” And when he says: God hears those who praise Him, then say: Our Lord, praise be to You, God hears you, for God said on the tongue of His Prophet: God hears those who Praise Him, then when the Imam says “Allahu Akbar” and prostrates, “Allahu Akbar” and prostrate, for the Imam prostrates before you and rises before you.” The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He, peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Then the same is true. If it is at the time of sitting, let the first thing one of you say should be: The good greetings, the good greetings, the prayers.” To God, peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God’s mercy and blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that “Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"752","754 Abu Al-Ash’ath Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam Al-Ajli Al-Basri, who said: Al-Mu’tamir narrated to us, saying: I heard my father speaking, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Ghallab, who is Yunus bin Jubayr, on the authority of Hattan bin Abdullah, that they prayed with Abu Musa, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him And he said: “If it is at the time of sitting, let it be the first thing one of you says: Good greetings and prayers are for God. Peace be upon you, O Prophet. By God’s mercy and blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God, I bear witness that there is no god but God, alone with no partner, and that Muhammad His servant and Messenger\ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"753","755 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, and Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to teach us the Tashahhud just as he taught us the Qur’an, and he used to say: “Blessed greetings and good prayers.” To God, peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God’s mercy and blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God, and I bear witness that there is no god but God. “I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"754","756 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard Ayman, who is Ibn Nabul, saying: Abu Al-Zubayr told me. On the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to teach us the Tashahhud just as he taught us a surah from the Qur’an, “In the name of God, and by God Greetings to God, and prayers and good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God’s mercy and blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. “I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. I ask God for Paradise and I seek refuge in God from Hell.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"755","757 Al-Haytham bin Ayyub Al-Talqani told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Abdul-Rahman bin Awf told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah bin Abdullah bin Masoud, on the authority of his father, who said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform the two rak’ahs As if he was on his knees.” I said: “Until he gets up.” He said: “That is what he wants.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"756","758 Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, on the authority of Ibn Buhaynah, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He prayed and stood up during the Shaf’ in which he wanted to sit, so he continued in his prayer until, when he was in the last part, his prayer He prostrated two prostrations before he said the salutation, then he saluted.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"757","759 Abu Dawud Sulayman bin Saif told us, he said: Wahb bin Jarir told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, on the authority of Ibn Buhaynah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “prayed and stood up in the two rak’ahs, so they praised him and he went on, and when he finished During his prayer, he prostrated two prostrations, then gave the salutation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"758","760 Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir bin Dinar informed us, saying: Baqiyya bin Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Buhair, on the authority of Khalid bin Maadan, on the authority of Kathir ibn Murrah, on the authority of Amr ibn Absa, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever builds a mosque to be remembered God is in him, God will build a house for him in Paradise.”"
"759","761 Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, saying: Anba Abdullah, meaning Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “One of the signs of the Hour is that people will show off in the mosques.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"760","762 Ali bin Hajar informed us, he said: Ali bin Mushar informed us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I used to recite the Qur’an to my father on the highway. So, when I recited the prostration, he prostrated, and I said: O my father, should I prostrate on the road? He said: I heard Abu Dharr say: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the first mosque placed on earth. He said: “The mosque.” The Sacred Mosque.” So I said: Then which? He said: “Al-Aqsa Mosque.” I said: How much between them? He said: “Forty years, and the earth is yours as a mosque, so where “Whatever prayer takes you away from, pray.”"
"761","763 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Ma’abad bin Abbas, that Maimuna, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Pray in the Mosque of the Messenger, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Prayer in it.” “It is better than a thousand prayers in any other mosque, except the Kaaba Mosque.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"762","764 Qutaibah bin Sa’id told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered May God bless him and grant him peace. The house was closed to him, Osama bin Zaid, Bilal, and Uthman bin Talha. They closed it for them, and when they opened, I was the first to enter. So I met Bilal and asked him: Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray there? He said: “Yes, he prayed between the two Yemeni pillars.”"
"763","765 Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Mushar told me, he said: Saeed bin Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Rabi’a bin Yazid, On the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Ibn Al-Daylami, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he is Ibn Al-Aas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace “When Solomon Ibn Dawud built the Mosque of Jerusalem, he asked God for three things: He asked God for a ruling that coincided with his ruling, and he was given it, and he asked God A kingdom that no one after him should have, so he was given it. He asked God, when he finished building the mosque, that no one should come to it without occupying it except to pray in it. To free him from his sin as on the day his mother gave birth to him.”"
"764","766 Kathir ibn Ubaid al-Humsi informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Harb told us, on the authority of al-Zubaidi, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah ibn Abd The Most Gracious, the client of the Jahanis, who were among Abu Hurairah’s companions, said that they heard Abu Hurairah say: “Prayer in the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” A salutation is better than a thousand prayers, in all other mosques except the Sacred Mosque, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was the last of the prophets. And his mosque is the last of the mosques.” Abu Salamah and Abu Abdullah said: We have no doubt that Abu Hurairah was saying about the hadith of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace and blessings of God be upon him: We were prevented from asking Abu Hurairah to prove that hadith, so that when Abu Hurairah died, we mentioned that and blamed us. Should we not have spoken to Abu Hurairah about that, so that we can attribute it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, if he heard it from him while we are on the same page? That's when Abdullah bin Ibrahim bin Qarith sat with us, so we mentioned that hadith, which we overlooked from the text of Abu Hurairah, so he said to us Abdullah bin Ibrahim: I bear witness that I heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “For I am the last of the prophets. And it is the last of the mosques.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"765","767 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zaid He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What is between my house and my pulpit is one of the gardens of Paradise.”"
"766","768 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ammar al-Dahni, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The steps of this pulpit of mine are places in Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"767","769 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas, on the authority of Ibn Abi Saeed, on the authority of Abi Saeed, he said: Two men debated in the mosque that was founded on piety from the first day. One man said: It is the Mosque of Quba. The other said: It is the Mosque of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “This is my mosque.”"
"768","770 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He said: “Quba’ will come, riding and walking.”"
"769","771 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Muja’ bin Yaqoub told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sulayman al-Kirmani, he said: I heard Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif said: My father said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever goes out until he comes to this mosque, the Quba Mosque? So he prayed therein, and he had the equivalent of an Umrah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"770","772 Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “Journeys should only be made to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and Al-Aqsa Mosque.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"771","773 Hanad bin Al-Sirri told us, on the authority of a lieutenant, who is Ibn Amr, who said: Abdullah bin Badr told me, on the authority of Qays bin Talq, on the authority of his father. Talaq bin Ali said: We went out as a delegation to the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so we pledged allegiance to him and prayed with him and informed him that there was a pledge of allegiance in our land. For us, and we asked him to give him the surplus of his purification, so he called for water, performed ablution, and rinsed his mouth, then poured it for us as a remedy, and he commanded us, saying: “Come out.” So when you come to your land, break your pledge of allegiance, and sprinkle this water in its place, and take it as a place of worship.” So we said to him, “The country is far away.” The heat was intense and the water was drying up. He said: “Spread water over it, for it only adds good to it.” So we went out until we reached our country and broke our pledge of allegiance. Then We filled its place and made it a mosque, and we called the call to prayer. He said: And the monk is a man from Tayy. When he heard the call to prayer, he said: A call. Indeed, then he met one of our hills and we did not see him again. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"772","774 Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, on the authority of Abu al-Tayyah, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: When the Messenger of God came May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he camped outside the city in a neighborhood called Banu Amr bin Awf. He stayed there for fourteen nights, then He sent for a group of Banu al-Najjar, and they came with their swords drawn, as if I were looking at the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on his camel and riding Bakr, his servant, and the chiefs of Banu al-Najjar around him, until he reached the courtyard of Abu Ayyub, and he used to pray wherever prayer approached him, so he prayed in sitting places. The sheep. Then we were ordered to the mosque, and he sent for the chiefs of Banu al-Najjar, and they came. He said: “O Banu al-Najjar, make me eighth in this wall of yours.” They said: No. By God, we do not ask for its price except from God. Anas said: And there were the graves of the polytheists, and there were ruins in it, and there were palm trees in it. So he ordered The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “The graves of the polytheists were dug up, and the palm trees were cut down, and the ruins were leveled.” So, line up the palm trees. The direction of the mosque, and they made stones on its supports, and they began to move the rocks, while they were shaking while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with them and they say: O God, there is no good except the good of the Hereafter, so help the Ansar and the Muhajirah.”"
"773","775 Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Muammar and Yunus, they said: Al-Zuhri said: Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah informed me, Aisha and Ibn Abbas said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, descended on him, he began to throw his khamis on his face, and when he felt sad, He uncovered his face and said while doing so: “May God’s curse be upon the Jews and Christians. They have taken the graves of their prophets as places of worship.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"774","776 Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Aisha Umm Habibah and Umm Salamah mentioned a church they saw in Abyssinia that had pictures, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed Those are the ones who, when there was a righteous man among them and he died, they built a mosque over his grave and made those pictures. These are the worst of creation in the sight of God on the Day of Judgment. \resurrection\"""""
"775","777 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, he said: Al-Aswad bin Al-Ala bin Haritha Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Abu Salamah, who is Ibn Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “When he comes out “The man from his house to my mosque: there is a man whose good deeds are written, and there is a man whose bad deeds are erased.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"776","778 Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Abba Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “If the woman of one of you asks permission to go to the mosque, he should not prevent her.”"
"777","779 Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abba Yahya, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata’ told us, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever eats from this tree and says on the first day: garlic, then says: garlic, onions, and leeks, should not approach us in Our mosques, for angels are harmed by whatever humans are harmed by.”"
"778","780 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Hisham told us, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Maadan bin Abi Talha, that Omar bin Al-Khattab said: “You people eat from two trees that I see only These are two vile things, these onions and garlic. I have seen the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he smelled their scent from a man. He ordered him to be taken out to Al-Baqi’, whoever eats them, let him kill them cooked.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"779","781 Abu Dawud told us, he said: Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, she said: It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “If he wanted to seclude himself, he prayed the morning prayer, then he entered the place where he wanted to seclude himself, and he wanted to seclude himself.” He used to seclude himself during the last ten days of Ramadan, so he ordered and a tent to be put up for him, and Hafsa ordered and a tent to be put up for her, so when Zainab saw her tent She commanded, and a tent was made for her. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw that, he said: “By righteousness, they want.” So he did not seclude himself in Ramadan, and he secluded himself “The ten days of Shawwal”"
"780","782 Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “Saad was injured on the day of the ditch. A man from the Quraysh shot him. He threw him into Al-Akhal, and he was hit on him.” She means the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Peace be upon him, a tent in the mosque so that he may return soon."
"781","783 Qutaibah bin Sa’id informed us, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Amr bin Sulaym al-Zarqi, that he heard Abu Qatada said: “While we were sitting in the mosque, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us, carrying Umamah bint Abi Al-Aas bin Al-Rabi’, and her mother was Zainab, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and she was a girl. He carried her on his shoulders, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed. He said hello while it was on his shoulder, placing it when he bowed and putting it back when he stood, until he finished his prayer, doing that with it.”"
"782","784 Qutaibah bin Sa’id informed us, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, that he heard Abu Hurairah say: “He sent The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rode off before Najd and brought a man from Banu Hanifa, called Thumama bin Athal, the lord of the people of Al-Yamamah. So they tied him to one of the poles of the mosque, brief."
"783","784 Suleiman bin Dawud informed us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “During the Farewell Pilgrimage, he circumambulated on a camel receiving the pillar at Mahjin.”"
"784","785 Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed informed me, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his grandfather, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade the wearing of one’s hair on Friday before prayer, and the prohibition of buying and selling in the mosque.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"785","786 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade chanting poems in the mosque.”"
"786","787 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: Omar passed by Hassan bin Thabit While he was singing in the mosque, he noticed him and said: I sang while there was someone better than you, then he turned to Abu Hurairah and said: Did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Answer on my behalf. Oh God, support him with the Holy Spirit.” He said: Oh God, yes."
"787","788 Muhammad bin Wahb told us, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahim, he said: Zaid told me, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, On the authority of Jabir, he said: “A man came seeking a lost item in the mosque, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: No, I found it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"788","789 Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman and Muhammad bin Mansour told us, saying: Sufyan told us, he said: I said to Amr: Did you hear? Jabir, saying: “A man passed by in the mosque with arrows, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Take their arrows. He said: Yes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"789","790 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Isa bin Yunus, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: I entered Alqamah came to Abdullah bin Masoud, and he said to us: Are these people praying? We said: No. He said: Stand up and pray, so we went to stand behind him, so he placed one of us on his right and the other on his left, so he prayed without the call to prayer, and there was no call to prayer. “Iqama,” and when he bowed, he interlaced his fingers and placed them between his knees, and said: This is what I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, do. Abba Ishaq bin Ibrahim said: Al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman, he said: I heard Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, And Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah, mentioned something similar."
"790","791 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, on the authority of his uncle, that he saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, “lying down in the mosque, placing one of his legs over the other.”"
"791","792 Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he said: Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that “it was He slept while he was a single young man with no family during the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the mosque of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"792","794 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “A slug in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it.”"
"793","793 Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw spit in He rubbed the wall of the qibla, then turned to the people and said: “When one of you is praying, he should not spit on his face, for God is before his face.” \When he prays\"""""
"794","794 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw dirt in the direction of the mosque, so he rubbed it off with a pebble, and he forbade a man to spit in his hands, or His right, and he said: “He spits on his left, or under his left foot.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"795","795 Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Mansour told me, on the authority of Rabi’i, on the authority of Tariq bin Abdullah Al-Muharbi said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When you are praying, do not spit in front of your hands, nor on your right. And spit behind you or facing your left side, if it is empty, otherwise, then so on. And Yahya spit under his leg and rubbed it.”"
"796","796 Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, saying: Abba Abdullah, on the authority of Sa’id al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu al-Ala’ ibn al-Shakhir, on the authority of his father, he said: “I saw The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “suddened his throat and rubbed it with his left foot.”"
"797","797 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Aidh bin Habib, he said: Humaid al-Tawil told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: “He saw The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had phlegm in the direction of the mosque and became angry until his face turned red, so a woman from the Ansar got up and scratched it. And in its place it was placed in good manners. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: How good is this."
"798","798 Sulayman bin Ubayd Allah al-Ghaylani Basri told us, he said: Abu Amir told us, he said: Sulayman told us, on the authority of Rabi’ah, on the authority of Abd Al-Malik bin Saeed said: I heard Abu Humaid and Abu Usayd saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you enters When he enters the mosque, let him say: O God, open for me the doors of Your mercy, and when he goes out, let him say: O God, I ask You of Your bounty.”"
"799","799 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Aamir bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Amr bin Sulaym, on the authority of Abu Qatada, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you enters the mosque, he should perform two rak’ahs before sitting in it.”"
"800","800 Suleiman bin Dawud told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Yunus, he said: Ibn Shihab said: And Abd al-Rahman bin told me Ka'b bin Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ka'b, said: I heard Ka'b bin Malik narrating his speech when he lagged behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. In the Battle of Tabuk, he said: “And in the morning the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, arrived, and whenever he came from a journey, he would start at the mosque. He prayed two rak'ahs therein, then sat before the people. When he did that, those who were left behind came to him, and they began to apologize to him and swear to him, and they were a few people. Eighty men, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, accepted their public statements, pledged allegiance to them, asked forgiveness for them, and entrusted their secrets to God. Until I came, and when I greeted the angry man, he smiled and said: Come, so I came walking until I sat in front of him, and he said to me: What happened to you? Didn’t you buy? Your back? I said: O Messenger of God, by God, if I sat with other people of the world than you, I would think that I would escape his wrath. I have been given an argument, but by God I know that if I told you a false story today that you would be satisfied with on my behalf, God would soon make you angry with me. I told you a truthful story in which you find me to be pleased. In it, I hope for my successor in God. By God, I have never been stronger or easier than when I lagged behind you. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “As for this, it has been true. Arise until that judgment is decided upon you.” Then a brief summary continued."
"801","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam bin Ayan told us, on the authority of Shuaib, who said: Al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abu Hilal, he said: Marwan bin Othman told me, that Ubaid bin Hunayn told him, on the authority of Abu Saeed bin Al-Mu’alla, he said: “We used to go to bed in the morning. To the market at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we pass by the mosque and pray there.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"802","802 Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he said: “The angels pray over one of you as long as he remains in the prayer place in which he prayed, and that has not happened. O God, forgive him, O God, have mercy on him.”"
"803","803 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, saying: Bakr, meaning Ibn Mudar, told us, on the authority of Ayyash bin Uqba, that Yahya bin Maimun told him, He said: I heard Sahla Al-Saadi saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever is in a mosque waiting for prayer is in prayer.”"
"804","804 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace, “He forbade praying in the backs of camels.”"
"805","805 Al-Hasan bin Ismail bin Suleiman told us, he said: Abba Hushaym, he said: Abba Sayyar, on the authority of Yazid al-Faqir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The earth has been made for me a place of mosque and purification. Whenever a man from my nation attends prayer, he prays.”"
"806","806 Saeed bin Yahya bin Saeed the Umayyad told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abd Allah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that Umm Sulaym asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to come to her and pray in “So he came to her and she took out a mat and sprinkled it with water, so he prayed over it and they prayed with it.”"
"807","807 Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, meaning Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, on the authority of Maimuna, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “pray over the wine.”"
"808","808 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yaqoub bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Abu Hazim bin Dinar told me, that men came Sahl bin Saad Al-Saadi, and they were wondering in the pulpit what he was used to? So they asked him about that, and he said, “By God, I know what it is.” And I saw it the first day it was installed, and the first day the Messenger of God sat on it. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent to so-and-so, a woman whom he called Sahl, to see your servant, the carpenter, work for me. Sticks that I sit on when I speak to people. So I ordered him and he made them from the tamarisks of the forest, then he brought them and they were sent to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he ordered it to be put here, then I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying over it and saying “Allahu Akbar” while he was over it, then He bowed while he was on it, then the one who recited came down and prostrated at the origin of the pulpit and then returned. When he finished, he approached the people and said: “O people, I have done This is so that you may follow me and learn my prayer.”"
"809","809 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya, on the authority of Saeed bin Yasar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: I saw the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “He was praying on a donkey on his way to Khaybar.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Amr ibn Yahya did not follow up on what he said: He prays on a donkey. They only say he prays on his camel. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"810","810 Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Ismail bin Omar told us, he said: Dawud bin Qais told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that he saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “praying on a donkey while he was riding to Khaybar.” And the qiblah is behind him.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is a mistake, and the correct one is definite. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"811","811 Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, he said: Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: Haywa bin Shurayh told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked, in the Battle of Tabuk, “about the prayer’s sutrah,” and he said: Such as \back of the journey\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"812","812 Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he said: Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, “He used to focus the spear, then pray towards it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"813","813 Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Haritha ibn Mudharib, on the authority of Ali, he said: We saw the night of a full moon and not a single person among us was asleep, except for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for he was praying by a tree. And he prayed until morning.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"814","814 Ali bin Hajar and Ishaq bin Mansour informed us, saying: Abba Sufyan, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, on the authority of Sahl bin Abi Hathamah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you prays facing a sutrah, let him approach it, and not cut off.” Satan, may his prayers be upon him.”"
"815","815 Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin informed us of a reading from him, and I am listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim. He said: Malik told me, On the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the Kaaba, he, Osama bin Zaid, and Bilal, And Othman bin Talha Al-Hajbi, so he closed it on him. Abdullah said: I asked Bilal when he left, what did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, do? ? He said: “He placed a pillar on its left, two pillars on its right, and three pillars behind it, and the house at that time was on six pillars. Then he prayed and placed between him and the wall a space of about three cubits. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"816","816 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Humayd bin Hilal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you is standing and praying, then he should cover it if it is in his hands, such as At the end of the journey, if he does not have before him something like the end of the journey, then he should interrupt his prayer with the woman, the donkey, and the black dog.” I said. : What is the difference between black and yellow and red? He said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, just as you asked me, and he said: “The black dog is a devil.”"
"817","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Shu`bah and Hisham told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I said to Jabir bin Zaid: What He interrupts prayer? He said: Ibn Abbas used to say: “The menstruating woman and the dog.” Yahya said: Shu’bah narrated it."
"818","818 Muhammad bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Al-Zuhri told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told me, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “ Al-Fadl and I came on our own donkey, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was leading the people in prayer at Arafat. Then he mentioned a word that meant it, so we passed by. On some row, we went down and left it grazing, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not say anything to us.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"819","819 Abdul Rahman bin Khalid told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Ibn Juraij said: Muhammad bin Omar bin Ali informed us, on the authority of Abbas bin Ubayd Allah ibn Abbas, on the authority of Al-Fadl ibn Abbas, he said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, visited Abbas in our desert, and we have a female dog and a donkey.” She grazed, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the afternoon prayer while they were in front of him, but they were not deterred or delayed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"820","820 Abu Al-Ash’ath told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, that Al-Hakam informed him, he said: I heard Yahya speaking, On the authority of Suhayb, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas narrating that “he and a boy from Banu Hashim passed on a donkey in front of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” in the presence of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was praying, so they came down and entered with him and prayed, but he did not leave, and two maids came seeking From the Banu Abd al-Muttalib, they grabbed his knee and he panicked among them and did not leave.”"
"821","821 Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I was in the presence of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was praying, so if I wanted to get up, I hated to get up, so I would pass between... His hands slipped freely.”"
"822","822 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Nadr, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, that Zayd bin Khalid sent him to Abu Juhaim asks him, What did he hear from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as he passed in front of the person praying? Abu Juhaym said to me: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the one who passes in front of the praying person knew what he would have to do, he would have stopped for forty.” “It is better for him than for it to pass through his hands.”"
"823","823 Qutaibah bin Sa’id informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you is praying, let him not let anyone pass in front of him. If he refuses, let him fight him, for he is with him.” Al-Qurain"
"824","824 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Issa bin Yunus told us, he said: Abd al-Malik bin Abdul Aziz bin Jurayj told us, on the authority of Kathir bin Kathir, Makki, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, circumambulating the Kaaba seven days, then prayed. “Perform two rak’ahs with his shoes on the edge of the shrine, and there should be no one between him and the tawaf.”"
"825","824 Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “He prays at night while I lie lying between him and the qiblah on his bed. If he wants to pray the prayer, he wakes me up.” So I performed Witr.”"
